          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Enabling auditing and monitoring for email attachments and file transfers helps detect and investigate suspicious activity.",
          "passage_ids": [
            "T1566.001:mitigation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Network intrusion prevention systems can be used to block activity by scanning and removing malicious email attachments.",
          "passage_ids": [
            "T1566.001:mitigation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Blocking unknown or unused attachments by default, such as .scr, .exe, .pif, and .cpl files, prevents some attack vectors.",
          "passage_ids": [
            "T1566.001:mitigation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Using anti-spoofing and email authentication mechanisms like SPF, DKIM, and DMARC filters messages based on sender validity and integrity.",
          "passage_ids": [
            "T1566.001:mitigation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Applying user account management principles limits permissions for accounts interacting with email attachments to reduce the impact of malicious files.",
          "passage_ids": [
            "T1566.001:mitigation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Training users to identify social engineering techniques and spearphishing emails is a mitigation strategy.",
          "passage_ids": [
            "T1566.001:mitigation"
          ]
        }
      ],
